event: template_sections
data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"header","type":"template","content":"LEGAL NOTICE\n(Under Section 138 read with Section 141 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881)\n\nDate: 04 May 2026\nBy Registered Post A.D. / Speed Post / UPC\n\nTo,\nMr. Vikram Yadav\nPlot 7, Anisabad, Patna - 800002\n\nFrom,\nMr. Ankit Sharma\nThrough: Adv. Rohit Kumar, Advocate\nChamber 15, Civil Court Compound, Patna - 800001","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"subject_line","type":"template","content":"Subject: Statutory Demand Notice under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 — Cheque No. 458823 dated 2026-03-25 for Rs. 350000/- (Three Lakh Fifty Thousand only) drawn on HDFC Bank, Boring Road Branch, Patna — dishonoured on 2026-04-04\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nUnder instructions from and on behalf of my client, Mr. Ankit Sharma, I hereby serve upon you this statutory notice under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, and call upon you to note as under:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That my client had advanced a friendly loan of Rs. 3,50,000/- (Rupees Three Lakh Fifty Thousand only) to the noticee on 15.11.2025 for a period of four months. The said loan was acknowledged in writing by the noticee vide acknowledgment dated 15.11.2025, whereby the noticee undertook to repay the entire loan amount within the stipulated period.\n\n2. That towards discharge of the aforesaid liability, the noticee Mr. Vikram Yadav issued Cheque No. 458823 dated 25.03.2026 for Rs. 3,50,000/- (Rupees Three Lakh Fifty Thousand only) drawn on HDFC Bank, Boring Road Branch, Patna in favour of my client.\n\n3. That the said cheque was duly presented by my client to his bankers for collection on 02.04.2026. However, the said cheque was returned dishonoured vide the bank's return memo dated 04.04.2026 with the endorsement 'Funds Insufficient'.\n\n4. That the dishonour of the aforesaid cheque constitutes a criminal offence under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, which is punishable with imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine which may extend to twice the amount of the cheque, or with both.\n\n5. That as per the proviso (b) to Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, the payee or the holder in due course of the cheque is required to make a demand for the payment of the said amount of money by giving a notice in writing to the drawer of the cheque within thirty days of the receipt of information by him from the bank regarding the return of the cheque as unpaid.\n\n6. That my client received the information regarding dishonour of the said cheque on 04.04.2026, and this notice is being served well within the statutory period of thirty days as mandated under the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881.\n\n7. That the noticee is legally bound and liable to make payment of the cheque amount along with interest and costs, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate criminal proceedings against the noticee under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881 before the competent Court of Law."},{"section_id":"demand_clause","type":"template","content":"DEMAND\n\nYou are hereby called upon to make payment of the said sum of Rs. 350000/- (Three Lakh Fifty Thousand only) to my client within a period of fifteen (15) days from the date of receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate criminal proceedings against you under Section 138 of the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, before the competent Magistrate having jurisdiction, at your risk, cost, and consequences.\n\nPlease note that under Section 138, if you fail to make payment within 15 days of receipt of this notice, my client shall file a criminal complaint within 30 days thereafter, and upon conviction you shall be liable to imprisonment for a term which may extend to two years, or with fine which may extend to twice the amount of the cheque, or with both.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"closing","type":"template","content":"A copy of this notice is retained in my office for record and further legal action.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n_________________________\nAdv. Rohit Kumar\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. BCB/3127/2016\nChamber 15, Civil Court Compound, Patna - 800001\n\n(Counsel for Mr. Ankit Sharma)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

